WEBVTT

1.1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.877
Step 1. Open the Medication Request form.

1.2
00:00:02.877 --> 00:00:07.491
Here you copy medicines from the patient's past prescriptions into a new

1.3
00:00:07.491 --> 00:00:12.413
prescription. Select the Medication quick action on the Overview tab.

2.1
00:00:12.413 --> 00:00:16.843
Step 2. Open the medication history. Select Medication History.

2.2
00:00:16.843 --> 00:00:20.957
The button is on the form only when you create a prescription,

2.3
00:00:20.957 --> 00:00:22.917
not when you edit one.

3.1
00:00:22.917 --> 00:00:25.431
Step 3. Select the past records.

3.2
00:00:25.431 --> 00:00:30.313
Past Prescriptions lists the patient's medicines from all encounters.

3.3
00:00:30.313 --> 00:00:38.728
Select each record that you want, then select Add Selected.

4.1
00:00:38.728 --> 00:00:41.039
Step 4. Complete the new rows.

4.2
00:00:41.039 --> 00:00:46.192
A medicine from Past Prescriptions comes with its dosage and other details,

4.3
00:00:46.192 --> 00:00:49.303
and Care records you as its requester.

5.1
00:00:49.303 --> 00:00:52.825
Step 5. Save the medicines. Select Save Changes.

5.2
00:00:52.825 --> 00:00:56.437
The added medicines are part of the new prescription,

5.3
00:00:56.437 --> 00:00:59.526
and the earlier records do not change.
